---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HVAC Training Solutions | Learn HVAC with Ron Walker"
  description="New to HVAC? Explore Ron Walker's 27-module online HVAC Boot Camp, see how the existing course works, review pricing, and watch a free teaching sample."
>
  <div class="marketing-home">
    <section class="home-hero refreshed-hero">
      <div class="home-hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Online HVAC training for your first step</p>
          <h1>New to HVAC? <span>Build a foundation you can explain.</span></h1>
          <p class="home-hero-lead">Start with how systems move heat, then work through the tools, safety, airflow, electricity, and equipment you will encounter in the trade. Ron Walker's HVAC Boot Camp gives beginners a structured place to start.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">Explore HVAC Boot Camp</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/try-boot-camp/">Watch a free teaching sample</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-fineprint">Online study · 27 modules in the current course · Textbook purchased separately</p>
        </div>

        <aside class="hero-lesson-card" aria-label="Free teaching sample">
          <div class="hero-lesson-top"><span class="preview-pill">Free teaching sample</span><span>HVAC basics · Moving heat</span></div>
          <p class="hero-lesson-label">Start with one idea</p>
          <h2>An air conditioner moves heat. It does not make cold.</h2>
          <div class="heat-flow-graphic" aria-label="Heat moves from warm indoor air into the evaporator coil">
            <div><small>Warmer</small><strong>Indoor air</strong></div>
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            <div><small>Colder</small><strong>Evaporator coil</strong></div>
          </div>
          <p>See how Ron explains a core HVAC idea, then review the course you can enroll in today.</p>
          <a href="/try-boot-camp/">Watch Ron teach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <small class="preview-disclosure">The paid Boot Camp has 27 modules in Moodle with textbook reading, videos, and quizzes.</small>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="audience-section" aria-labelledby="choose-path">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Find what brought you here</p>
        <h2 id="choose-path">Two ways to use this site.</h2>
        <div class="audience-grid">
          <a class="audience-card" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">
            <span class="audience-icon" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <span><strong>I'm exploring an HVAC career</strong><small>See what Boot Camp teaches, how the current course works, and what it costs.</small><b>Explore Boot Camp →</b></span>
          </a>
          <a class="audience-card" href="/resources/">
            <span class="audience-icon resource-icon" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <span><strong>I'm looking up a technical question</strong><small>Find practical articles on refrigerant recovery, pressure and temperature, superheat, and more.</small><b>Browse free resources →</b></span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section soft-section" aria-labelledby="course-today">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The course available today</p><h2 id="course-today">A structured start, from heat basics to heat pumps.</h2><p>HVAC Boot Camp is an existing online course for beginners. Its 27 modules use textbook reading, Ron's video instruction, and quizzes in Moodle. The textbook is an additional purchase.</p></div>
        <div class="foundation-grid">
          <article><span>01 / Fundamentals</span><h3>Understand the system</h3><p>Heat, refrigeration, matter, safety, and the tools used around HVAC equipment.</p></article>
          <article><span>02 / Systems</span><h3>Follow the air and refrigerant</h3><p>Air distribution, refrigerant management, startup, charging, and indoor air quality.</p></article>
          <article><span>03 / Electrical</span><h3>Make sense of controls</h3><p>Electricity, motors, controls, diagrams, codes, and basic troubleshooting.</p></article>
          <article><span>04 / Equipment</span><h3>Keep building</h3><p>Heating systems, heat pumps, and mechanical troubleshooting.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="section-action"><a class="button button-dark" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">See the full curriculum</a><a class="text-link-dark" href="/how-it-works/">How studying works today →</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="course-sample">
      <div class="page-shell preview-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">See the course before you decide</p>
          <h2 id="course-sample">Hear Ron teach. Explore what Boot Camp covers.</h2>
          <p>Start with a free public teaching sample, then browse the actual 27-module course outline. You can see the topics, the textbook requirement, the study format, and the price before enrolling.</p>
          <p class="preview-boundary"><strong>The current course:</strong> study the textbook, watch Ron's videos, and complete quizzes in Moodle. You will still need supervised practice to develop field skills.</p>
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/try-boot-camp/">Watch a free sample</a>
        </div>
        <div class="preview-steps" aria-label="Topics in the current Boot Camp">
          <div><span>1</span><strong>Fundamentals</strong><small>Heat and refrigeration</small></div>
          <div><span>2</span><strong>Systems</strong><small>Airflow and refrigerant</small></div>
          <div><span>3</span><strong>Electrical</strong><small>Motors and controls</small></div>
          <div><span>4</span><strong>Heating</strong><small>Equipment and operation</small></div>
          <div><span>5</span><strong>Heat pumps</strong><small>Continuing the path</small></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section instructor-section" aria-labelledby="meet-ron">
      <div class="page-shell instructor-grid">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Meet your instructor</p><h2 id="meet-ron">Learn the why with Ron Walker.</h2><p>Ron's lessons connect the science to what technicians observe. Watch a public refrigeration cycle lesson to see his teaching style before deciding whether Boot Camp fits.</p><div class="section-action"><a class="button button-light" href="/about/">Meet Ron</a><a class="text-link-light" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=27uCRQ3B8r4">Watch on YouTube ↗</a></div></div>
        <div class="video-frame"><iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/27uCRQ3B8r4?rel=0" title="Basic Refrigeration Cycle lesson by Ron Walker" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="ready-next">
      <div class="page-shell home-next">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Ready to look closer?</p><h2 id="ready-next">Know the course and the cost before you decide.</h2><p>Pay $479 in full, or $97 now plus six monthly payments of $97 ($679 total). The textbook is purchased separately. Online study builds a foundation; supervised field experience is still essential.</p></div>
        <div class="home-next-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/pricing/">See pricing and enrollment</a><a class="button button-outline-dark" href="/contact/">Ask a question</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
